---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import "../../styles/company-profile.css";
import { sitePath } from "../../app/config/site";
const base = sitePath();
---
<SiteLayout title="Our Story | Eshwar Home Products" description="The story of Eshwar Home Products: a millet-store idea in 2023, devotion to the family deity Eshwaran and a neighbourhood pantry in Perambur." current="profile">
<div class="company-profile cp-subpage cp-story-page"><section class="cp-subhero"><div class="container"><a class="cp-back-link cp-back-light" href={sitePath("profile/")}>← Company Profile</a><p class="cp-eyebrow">02 · OUR STORY</p><h1>Rooted in devotion.<br/><em>Made for everyday kitchens.</em></h1><p>A local idea shaped by a wish to offer something distinctive on a familiar street.</p></div></section>
<section class="container cp-story-intro"><div class="cp-story-year"><span>THE IDEA</span><strong>2023</strong><small>The year the concept began</small></div><div class="cp-prose"><p class="cp-eyebrow">WHERE IT BEGAN</p><h2>Not just another provision store.</h2><p>In 2023, the thought began with a simple observation: many provision stores already served the same streets. The aim was to create something distinctive rather than become just another conventional store.</p><p>The idea of opening a millet-focused shop felt meaningful. The growing public attention around millets in India also encouraged the thought. The founders saw an opportunity to make traditional grains and pantry products easier for people in the neighbourhood to discover.</p><p>That idea became Eshwar Home Products, a store named with devotion after the family deity, Eshwaran (Lord Shiva).</p></div></section>
<section class="cp-story-emblem"><div class="container cp-emblem-inner"><img src={base+"images/brand/eshwar-home-products-logo.png"} alt="Eshwar Home Products official Rudraksha and Trishul emblem" width="320" height="183" loading="lazy"/><div><p class="cp-eyebrow">THE MEANING IN OUR EMBLEM</p><h2>A devotional identity, carried into daily service.</h2><p>The Rudraksha and Trishul emblem gives a visual expression to the store’s spiritual connection. The values we associate with that identity are honesty, gratitude and care.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="container cp-story-values"><p class="cp-eyebrow">WHAT GUIDES US</p><h2>Our values.</h2><div class="cp-value-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Honesty</h3><p>Clear answers about products, pack sizes and availability.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Gratitude</h3><p>Appreciation for the customers and neighbourhood that support the store.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Care</h3><p>Personal guidance and a welcoming experience for everyday pantry needs.</p></article></div><p class="cp-story-note">Our continuing focus is to serve the neighbourhood with traditional rice, millets and pantry essentials. We have not published additional dated milestones or formal future targets.</p><a class="cp-button cp-button-dark" href={sitePath("products/")}>Explore the pantry ↗</a></section></div>
</SiteLayout>
